hadiths[65]{hadithnumber,text}:
"984","`Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` when we came to Madinah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between me and Sa’d bin Rabi’ (may Allah be pleased with him). So Sa’d bin Rabi’ said (to me), “I am the wealthiest among the Ansar, (therefore) I will give you half of my wealth, and you may choose whichever of my two wives you like; I will divorce her for you, and when her waiting period is over, you may marry her.” (Ibrahim bin Abdur Rahman, the narrator, said) So Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, “I do not need this. (Just tell me) is there any market here where trade is conducted?” He replied, “Yes, there is a market called Qainuqa’.” (So) in the morning, Abdur Rahman went to that market and brought back some cheese and ghee. (The narrator) says that after that, he started going daily. After a few days, Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) came (to the service of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was a trace of yellow (scent) on his clothes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, “Have you married?” He replied, “Yes.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, “To whom?” He replied, “To an Ansari woman.” So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, “How much dowry did you give her?” He replied, “A gold date-stone’s weight,” or he said, “a gold date-stone.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, “Give a wedding feast, even if it is with only one goat.”"
"985","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. So whoever leaves that in which he suspects there is sin, he will also leave that which is clearly and openly sinful. And whoever dares to do that in which there is doubt of sin, soon he will fall into that which is clearly sinful. And sins are the protected pastures of Allah Almighty; whoever grazes around the pasture (i.e., sins), soon he will enter into that pasture as well.”"
"986","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that Utbah bin Abi Waqqas had made a will to his brother (the conqueror of Persia) Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the son of Zam’ah’s slave woman is mine, so you should take him into your custody. Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when the year of the conquest of Makkah came, Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) took him and said, “This is my nephew; my brother made a will to me about him.” So, ‘Abd bin Zam’ah stood up and said, “He is my brother and the son of my father’s slave woman.” Then both of them came to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “O Messenger of Allah! This is my nephew; my brother made a will to me about him.” (‘Abd) bin Zam’ah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “He is my brother, the son of my father’s slave woman, and was born on his bed.” So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O ‘Abd bin Zam’ah! The boy will go to you.” After that, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The child belongs to the (legal) owner of the bed, and the adulterer gets nothing but stones.” After that, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Umm al-Mu’minin Sawdah bint Zam’ah (may Allah be pleased with her) (his wife): “Observe veil from him.” Because the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw some resemblance to Utbah in the boy. Thus, Umm al-Mu’minin Sawdah (may Allah be pleased with her) did not see the boy until she met Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"987","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): Some people said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Some men bring us meat (to sell), and we do not know whether they have recited Bismillah over it or not."" So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Recite Bismillah over it yourselves and eat."""
"988","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""A time will come upon the people when a man will not care whether he acquires wealth through lawful means or unlawful means."""
"989","Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib رضي الله عنه and Zaid bin Arqam رضي الله عنه say: We used to trade during the time of the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم, so we asked the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم about sarf (for example, exchanging rupees for rupees). He صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""If it is hand to hand (i.e., cash), then it is permissible, and if it is on credit, then it is not permissible."""
"990","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission from the Commander of the Faithful, Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), (to meet him), but he was not granted permission. (At that time) Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was occupied with some work. So Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) returned. Then when Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) became free, he said, ""I heard the voice of Abdullah bin Qais (Abu Musa Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him), grant him permission."" So the people said, ""He has already gone back."" Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) called him again (and asked, ""Why did you return?""). He replied, ""We were commanded to do so."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Present a witness for this."" So he went to the gathering of the Ansar and asked them. The Ansar said, ""The testimony for this will be given by Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who is the youngest among us."" So he took him (to Umar), and he testified (that it was the command of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him). Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""This command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) remained hidden from me because I was busy traveling in the markets for trade."""
"991","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever wishes that his provision be expanded or his life be prolonged, he should maintain good relations with his relatives."""
"992","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he took “barley bread” and “fat” to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), and (at that time) the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) had mortgaged his armor in Madinah with a Jew and had bought some barley for his family with it. (Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him) says: Indeed, I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) say: “The family of Muhammad does not have even a sa’ (measure) of wheat or any other grain left for the evening, even though he had nine wives.”"
"993","Sayyiduna Miqdam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No person has eaten food better than that earned by his own hands, and Allah's Prophet Dawud (peace be upon him) used to eat from what he earned with his own hands."""
"994","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on the person who is gentle and generous when selling, buying, and demanding his due."""
"995","´Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Among the people before you, the angels met the soul of a man and asked, 'Have you done any good deed?' He replied, '(Nothing special, but) I used to order my servants to forgive the debt of the one in difficulty and to be gentle in demanding from the wealthy.' "" The narrator stated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""So, they also let him go."""
"996","`Sayyiduna Hakim bin Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The seller and the buyer both have the option (to cancel the deal) as long as they do not separate,"" or he said, ""until they part from each other. If both speak the truth and make clear the defects and qualities (of the goods), then there will be blessing in their transaction. But if they lie and conceal defects, the blessing of their trade will be erased."""
"997","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): We used to get different types of mixed dates, so we would sell two sa's of them for one sa' (of good quality dates of the same kind). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not sell two sa's for one sa', nor two dirhams for one dirham (because this is usury)."""
"998","Sayyiduna Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I saw my father, who had bought a slave who practiced cupping, then he broke the cupping instruments of that slave. So I asked him (the reason for this), and he said that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking the price of a dog and the price of blood, and he (peace be upon him) also forbade branding and being branded (that is, writing names or making designs with kohl or indigo on the arm, etc.), and from taking and giving usury. And the Prophet (peace be upon him) cursed the image-maker."
"999","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""A false oath makes the wealth defective and erases the blessing."""
"1000","Sayyiduna Khabbab (may Allah be pleased with him) says: In the days of ignorance, I was a blacksmith and ‘As bin Wa’il owed me some money. I used to go to ‘As to demand my debt. Once, ‘As said to me, “I will not give it to you until you deny the Prophethood of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).” I said, “Even if Allah gives you death and then resurrects you after death, I will never deny the Prophethood of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).” ‘As said, “Then leave me until I die and am resurrected, because at that time I will have wealth and children, and I will pay your debt.” Upon this, these verses (Surah Maryam: 77, 78) were revealed: “O Prophet! Have you seen the one who denies Our verses and says, ‘Surely, I will be given wealth and children (if I am resurrected after death)?’”"
"1001","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): A tailor invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to a meal which he had prepared for him, so I also went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to that meal. Bread and broth containing green gourd (long bottle gourd) and dried meat were placed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) searching for pieces of gourd in the bowl from here and there, so from that day I began to like gourd."
"1002","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a battle, and my camel became sluggish and tired, so I lagged behind. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and called out: ""Jabir!"" I replied, ""Yes."" He asked, ""How are you?"" I said, ""My camel is slow and has become tired, so I have fallen behind."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted and struck it with his stick. Then he said to me, ""Now mount it."" So I mounted it, and (the camel became so fast that) indeed I had to restrain it from overtaking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""Have you married?"" I replied, ""Yes."" He asked, ""Did you marry a virgin or a previously married woman?"" I replied, ""A previously married woman."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Why did you not marry a young virgin so that you could play with her and she could play with you?"" I replied, ""I have some younger sisters, so I wanted to marry a woman who would gather them together, comb their hair, and look after them."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Well, when you reach your wife, enjoy (intimacy with) her thoroughly."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Will you sell your camel?"" I replied, ""Yes."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought the camel from me for one uqiyah (of gold or silver). After that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached (Medina) before me, and I arrived in the morning. Then we went to the mosque, and we found the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the door of the mosque. He said, ""Have you just arrived?"" I replied, ""Yes."" He said, ""Leave your camel and go into the mosque and pray two rak‘ahs."" So I prayed, and then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) to weigh out one uqiyah (of gold or silver) for me, and he weighed it out for me generously. As I was about to return home, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Call him to me."" I thought to myself, ""Now I will get my camel back,"" though I disliked this very much. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Take your camel and its price as well."""
"1003","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) bought some sick camels from a man. That man had a partner in this business as well. So that man's partner came to Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) and, by way of apology, said: ""My partner has sold you sick camels; he did not recognize you."" Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""Alright, you may take them back."" Then he said: ""Leave them, we are content with the decision of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), because (he said): 'One's illness does not transfer to another.'"""
"1004","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that Abu Taybah performed cupping for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace be upon him) gave him a sa’ of dates and ordered his owner to reduce his tax."
"1005","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once had cupping done, and he gave wages to the one who performed the cupping for him. If this wage had been unlawful, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would never have given it."
"1006","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she bought a cushion which had pictures on it. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw it, he stood at the door and did not enter the house. (Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, says) When I saw the expression of displeasure on the blessed face of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I repent before Allah and His Messenger. What sin have I committed?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""What is this cushion?"" I replied, ""I bought it for you so that you may sit on it and lean against it."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those who make these pictures will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them, 'Give life to what you have created.'"" Furthermore, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels do not enter a house in which there are pictures."""
"1007","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that we were on a journey with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and I was riding a hot-tempered camel belonging to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). That camel would not stay under my control and would go ahead of all the people, so Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) would scold it and make it fall back, but then it would go ahead again, and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) would again scold it and make it fall back. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Sell this camel to me."" He replied, ""O Messenger of Allah! It is yours."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""(No, not like that) Sell it to me."" So he sold that camel to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abdullah! The camel is yours, do with it as you wish."" (That is, he gave it to him as a gift.)"
"1008","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he often suffered loss in buying and selling. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you buy and sell, say: (i.e., in buying and selling) there should be no deception or loss."""
"1009","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out during the day. He was not talking to me, nor was I talking to him, until he reached the market of Banu Qaynuqa. Then he sat in the courtyard of the house of Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: ""Where is the child, where is the child?"" But Fatimah al-Zahra (may Allah be pleased with her) kept Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) back for a little while. I thought she was dressing him or giving him a bath. After that, he came running, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced him, kissed him, and prayed: ""O Allah! Love him, and love those who love him."""
"1010","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An army will come with the intention of attacking the Ka'bah, and when they reach the plain of Bayda', all the people will be swallowed up by the earth."" (Umm al-Mu'mineen) says: I asked, O Messenger of Allah! How will all the people be swallowed up, even though among them will be those who have their markets and some people who are not of them? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""All the people will be swallowed up, but they will be resurrected according to their intentions."""
"1011","Narrated Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was once in the market when a man called out, ""O Abu al-Qasim!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned towards him. The man said, ""I was calling that person, not you."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya (nickname)."""
"1012","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that during the time of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), people used to buy grain from caravan people. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would send a man to them who would prohibit them from selling that grain at that very place until they had brought it to the place where grain is sold (i.e., the market). And Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) also said that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling grain or foodstuff at the same time it is purchased, without taking possession of it (and moving it to another place)."
"1013","It was asked from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) about the attribute of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which is mentioned in the Torah. He said, ""Alright! By Allah, the praise of him in the Qur'an is of the same kind as some of the praise in the Torah (the content in the Torah is of this kind): 'O Prophet! We have sent you as a witness over the religion of truth, as a bearer of glad tidings to the believers, as a warner to the disbelievers, and as a guardian for the unlettered. You are My servant and My messenger. I have named you Al-Mutawakkil. He is neither ill-tempered nor one who raises his voice in the markets, nor does he repay evil with evil, but rather he forgives and shows mercy. Allah will not cause him to die until He straightens a crooked religion through him so that they say (with certainty) La ilaha illallah, and through him, blind eyes, deaf ears, and heedless hearts are opened.'"""
"1014","Narrated Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): When (my father) Abdullah bin Amr bin Haram (may Allah be pleased with him) was martyred, he had some debt. So I requested the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to intercede so that some of the debt might be forgiven. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expressed this wish to those people, but they did not agree. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""Go and separate your dates into different heaps. Keep the Ajwa dates separate and the 'Adhq Zaid separate, then call me."" So I did that, and after that I called the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He came and sat on or among the dates. Then he said: ""Now measure out and give to the creditors."" So I started measuring and giving to them until I had paid off all the debt, and my dates remained as they were, as if nothing had been diminished from them."
"1015","Sidna Miqdam bin Ma'dikarib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Measure your grain, there will be blessing in it for you."""
"1016","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Ibrahim (peace be upon him) declared Makkah a sanctuary and prayed for blessings for it, and I have declared Madinah a sanctuary just as Ibrahim (peace be upon him) declared Makkah a sanctuary, and I have prayed for blessings in the 'Mudd' and 'Saa'' of Madinah just as Ibrahim (peace be upon him) prayed for Makkah."""
"1017","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` those who used to sell grain during the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) without measuring or weighing it, I saw that they were beaten because they were not to sell it until they had taken it to their homes (warehouses and other places of storage)."
"1018","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that anyone should sell grain before taking possession of it (i.e., before it reaches his store, shop, warehouse, etc.). Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) was asked the reason for this (prohibition), so he replied: This is like selling money for money, because the grain is not delivered at that time (until it comes into his store, warehouse, or shop, etc.)."
"1019","Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Selling gold for gold, wheat for wheat, dates for dates, and barley for barley is usury, except when it is equal for equal and hand to hand, then it is permissible. (Note: Selling 24-carat gold for 22-carat gold in equal weight is also usury.)"""
"1020","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that any townsman should sell the goods of a desert-dweller (outsider), and that the seller should not be told a higher price than the buyer’s price so that he may not sell, while the one telling does not intend to buy himself. And no person should sell over the sale of his brother, nor should he send a marriage proposal to a woman after his brother has already proposed to her, and no woman should seek to have her (Muslim) co-wife divorced with the intention that what is in her co-wife’s mouth may come into her own mouth."
"1021","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man declared his slave free after his death, but he himself became destitute and needed money. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) took hold of the slave’s hand and said: “Who will buy this slave from me?” Accordingly, Na’eem bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) bought him for such and such amount. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) gave that price to his owner."
"1022","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the sale of Habal al-Habalah. This sale was prevalent in the days of ignorance in such a way that a person would buy a she-camel and set the payment term as follows: when this she-camel gives birth, and then the offspring in her womb grows up and gives birth (then I will pay the price)."
"1023","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever buys a goat whose udder has been withheld (from milking), and he milks the goat—if he is pleased, he should keep it, and if he is displeased, he should return it and give one sa’ of dates in exchange for the milk."""
"1024","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a slave-girl commits adultery and it is proven against her, she should be punished and not just reprimanded. If she commits adultery again, she should be punished again and not just reprimanded. Then if she commits adultery a third time, she should be sold, even if it is for a rope of hair."""
"1025","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not meet the caravans bringing grain on the way, but let them come to the town, and no townsman should sell for a (Bedouin) outsider."" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) was asked, ""What does it mean that no townsman should sell for an outsider?"" He replied, ""It means that he should not act as a broker for him."""
"1026","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""None of you should sell over the sale of another, and do not go forth to meet the goods (of traders) until they reach the market (and are sold there)."""
"1027","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the sale of Muzabana, and Muzabana is to sell dried dates by measure in exchange for fresh dates, and to sell fresh grapes by measure in exchange for dried grapes."
"1028","Narrated from Sayyiduna Malik bin Aws (may Allah be pleased with him) that he needed change for one hundred gold dinars. (He says that) Sayyiduna Talha bin Ubaidullah called for him and both of them discussed the matter until he agreed, and he began to turn the gold dinars over in his hand. After that, he said, ""Wait for a while (O Malik bin Aws), by Allah! Do not leave Talha until you have taken the change from him (because) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Selling gold for gold is usury except when it is hand to hand...' and he narrated the entire hadith which has already been mentioned before."""
"1029","Narrated Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not sell gold for gold except equal in weight (i.e., give as much gold as you take back), and (similarly) do not sell silver for silver except equal in weight. But you may buy and sell gold for silver and silver for gold as you wish."""
"1030","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not sell gold for gold except equal in weight, with neither side being more or less; and do not sell silver for silver except equal in weight, with neither side being more or less; and do not sell (gold or silver) with one side being cash and the other deferred."""
"1031","´Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) says that exchanging dinar for dinar and dirham for dirham (in equal amounts) is permissible. It was said to him that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) does not hold this view (i.e., he permits selling with an increase or decrease). So Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him) said that I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): Did you hear this from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or did you see it in the Book of Allah? Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) replied: I do not say anything from either of these two, and you know the hadith of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) better than I do. However, Sayyiduna Usama (may Allah be pleased with him) informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Riba (usury) is only in deferred payment."""
"1032","It was asked from Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib and Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with them) about (currency exchange business). Each of them said (about the other), ""He is better than me (ask him)."" After that, both of them said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling gold for silver on credit."
"1033","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruits until their ripeness becomes apparent, and (forbade) selling dates on the tree in exchange for dried dates. Then he said that Sayyiduna Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) informed me that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) later permitted the sale of ‘Ariyyah (dates on the trees) in exchange for fresh or dried dates, and did not permit it in any other case. (The meaning of ‘Ariyyah is that the fruit of a tree is given as charity to a poor person, then if his coming to the orchard causes inconvenience, the fruit of that tree is bought back from him by estimation.)"
"1034","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade selling fruits until they ripen, and that no type of them should be sold in exchange for anything except dirhams and dinars, except for ‘ariyah, for which it is permissible to sell them in exchange for fruits."
"1035","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, permitted the sale of ‘Araya on the condition that it is five wasq or less than five wasq."
"1036","Sayyiduna Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) says that during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), people used to sell fruits (before they ripened). Then, when the buyers would pick the fruits and the sellers would demand their price, the buyers would say that the fruit’s core had turned black and the fruit had gone bad, and they would mention other similar defects and quarrel. Therefore, when such cases became frequent before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he, due to these disputes, advised them: “Either suspend the sale (of fruits), or if not, then do not sell until the fruit’s soundness becomes apparent.”"
"1037","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruits before they become ripe. It was asked, ""What is meant by ripe?"" He replied: ""Until they become red or yellow and fit for eating."""
"1038","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruits before they reach “zuhw.” It was asked, “What is ‘zuhw’?” He said, “When they become red.” Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Tell me! If Allah Almighty destroys the fruits, then for what does one of you take his brother’s wealth?”"
"1039","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed a man over Khaybar, and he brought some ""Janib"" (a superior type of) dates to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him, ""Are all the dates of Khaybar like this (of such quality)?"" He replied, ""No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah! We exchange one sa' of these dates for two sa' of other dates, and sometimes we exchange two sa' of these dates for three sa' of other dates."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Do not do so. Instead, sell the inferior dates for dirhams, and then buy the superior dates with those dirhams."""
"1040","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade Muhaqala, Mukhadara, Mulamasa, Munabadhah, and Muzabana."
"1041","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that Hind, the mother of Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him), said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that Abu Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) is a miserly man, so is there any sin upon me if I take something from his wealth secretly? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""You and your son may take as much as is sufficient for you according to custom."" (The limit of what is customary was not specified so that it remains general, and due to this general specification, this narration is included under this chapter.)"
"1042","Narrated Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed the right of pre-emption in every undivided property, but if the boundaries are fixed and the ways are changed, then there is no pre-emption."
"1043","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Ibrahim (peace be upon him) migrated along with (his wife) Sarah (may Allah be pleased with her), and they reached a town where there was a king, one of the kings or (he said) a tyrant, one of the tyrants. It was reported to him that Ibrahim (peace be upon him) had come with a very beautiful woman. So he sent a man to ask: 'O Ibrahim, who is this woman with you?' Ibrahim (peace be upon him) replied: 'She is my sister.' (The messenger said: The king is calling this woman.) After that, Ibrahim said to Sarah (peace be upon her): 'There is no believer on the face of the earth except you and me.' Then Ibrahim (peace be upon him) sent Sarah to the king. (When she reached the king,) the king turned his attention towards her, so she performed ablution and stood up to pray, and said: 'O Allah, if I believe in You and Your Messenger, and if I have protected my private parts from everyone except my husband, then do not let this disbeliever overpower me.' As soon as she made this supplication, the disbeliever fell down and began to rub his foot on the ground. Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said that Sarah (peace be upon her), seeing this state, said: 'O Allah! If he dies, people will say that she killed the king.' Then his condition went away. He turned towards her again, but she got up, performed ablution, and started praying, and said: 'O Allah! If I believe in You and Your Messenger, and I have protected my private parts from everyone except my husband, then do not let this disbeliever overpower me.' (After this) the king again fainted, to the extent that if he died, people would say that she killed the king. Then again his condition subsided. Then the second or third time, he said to the people: 'You have brought me a human or a devil? Take her back to Ibrahim (peace be upon him) and also hand over Ajar (Hajar) to her.' So she returned to Ibrahim (peace be upon him) and said: 'Do you know that Allah has humiliated that disbeliever and has also sent a slave-girl (Hajar, peace be upon her) for service.'"""
"1044","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, soon the son of Maryam, ‘Isa (peace be upon him), will descend among the people. He will be a just ruler. He will break the cross, kill the swine, and abolish the jizya. Wealth will become so abundant that no one will accept it."""
"1045","Narrated from Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that a man came to him and said, ""O Abu al-Abbas (this was his kunyah)! I am a man whose livelihood depends on the work of my own hands, and I make these pictures."" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""I will tell you only what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that is: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Whoever makes a picture, Allah will punish him until he puts life into it, and he will never be able to put life into it.'"" Hearing this, the man sighed deeply and his face turned pale. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""Woe to you! If you must do this work, then make pictures of trees or things that do not have a soul."""
"1046","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""There are three persons for whom I will be an opponent on the Day of Resurrection: (1) The person who makes a covenant in My name and then breaks it; (2) The person who sells a free man and consumes his price; (3) The person who hires a laborer, gets the full work done from him, and then does not pay his wages."""
"1047","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in the year of the conquest of Makkah: “Indeed, Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) have forbidden the sale of alcohol, dead animals, and idols.” The people asked, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the fat of a dead animal? For it is used to caulk ships and is also unlawful.” Then at that time, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “May Allah destroy the Jews! When Allah made fat unlawful for them, they melted it, sold it, and consumed its price.”"
"1048","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking the price of a dog, the wages of prostitution, and the wages of soothsaying."
